               <msContents>
                  <msItem n="1" xml:id="MS_Gough_Liturg_5-item1">
                     <title key="work_13126" type="desc">Manual, Use of York</title>
                     <note>Fragmentary: beginning in the litany of the blessing of the font (fol. 1r) which is followed by the baptismal rite (fol. 6v); ad baptizandum infirmum in necessitate (fol. 8r), incomplete; marriage service (fol. 10r) and mass (fol. 12v), the former imperfect at the beginning, the latter including the canon (fol. 15r); ritual for the Last Sacraments (fol. 19r) with commendation and procession to the church (fol. 27r); formula of absolution (fol. 28r), blessing of bread (fol. 28v); burial service (fol. 36r) incomplete at the beginning, and separated from the previous part by an incomplete office of the dead (fol. 29r-35r).</note>
                     <note>Fol. 9 is an addition with English texts connected with the marriage service (banns, etc.)</note>
                    
                     <textLang mainLang="la" otherLangs="enm">Latin and Middle English</textLang>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
